<!--
    Named libc/POSIX aggregate types in the prototype tables (`option libctypes
    off|opaque`).

    The built-in prototype tables' type vocabulary is width-stable, so every
    aggregate pointer in them is spelled `void *`: `fopen` returns one, `fclose`
    takes one, `__uflow` takes one. That is honest about the width and silent
    about the pointee, and the pointee is the one thing a declaration actually
    knows.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture (the `option` command
    needs one before the first `load file`). Both passes clear it and load the
    same real x86-64 coreutils `fmt`, whose imports include `fclose`, `fopen` and
    `__uflow`.

    Pass 1 (`option libctypes off`, the shipped default) reproduces the opaque
    vocabulary: `fclose(void *)`, `void * fopen(...)`.

    Pass 2 (`option libctypes opaque`) spells the same slots by name: the gate is
    a load-time env bridge, so it is set BEFORE `load file` in each pass.

    The fixture carries DWARF, which gives the third function a COMPLETE
    `_IO_FILE` under a bare name the named table also mints a shell for. It
    prints identically in both passes, with its real field layout, because the
    libctypes shells are left INCOMPLETE and the DWARF importer completes one in
    place instead of colliding with it.

    The script restores the default in its last command: the gate is a process
    environment variable, and the corpus runs in one process.

    Assertions span the combined output of both passes.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option libctypes off</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/regglobal_fmt_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function fclose</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function fopen</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function get_prefix</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option libctypes opaque</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/regglobal_fmt_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function fclose</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function fopen</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function get_prefix</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option libctypes off</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
